WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did Broadway stuff.
-I did.

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did do Broadway stuff.
-I did.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.039
Well, when I was a struggling
actress at NYU drama school,

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was really determined
to make it.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:11.077 size:88% position:44%
So I got a -- I borrowed
somebody's Equity card,

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.212 line:92%
and I made a fake Equity card

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:16.116
so I could sneak into Actors'
Equity and go on auditions.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:20.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even -- And, so, because
they had auditions, open calls

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.154 size:84% position:42% line:92%
for big Broadway shows,

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was this big
new musical called "Smile,"

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they were casting girls,
you know, my age,

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.728
like 18 years old, to be the
stars of this Broadway musical.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did sneak in
with my fake Equity card,

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.499 line:92%
and I made it really far.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.234 size:78% position:39%
It was, like, singers
who could move well

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
was what was required,
and I love singing.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.104 size:78% position:39%
So, I did really well
on the singing part,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.107
and I made it down to the final,
final, final, final callback.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
But for the final,
final callback,

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.411 size:78% position:39%
where there were only
like 20 girls left,

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had to do the "dance" part
of the audition,

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.749 size:81% position:41%
and Miss Debbie Allen
was the choreographer.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we got to meet her.
-A famous...

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.053 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-A famous choreographer.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like the gold standard
of dance, really.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, so, she was just like --
You know, I was like,

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, my God.
This is could be my big break!

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've made it this far
with the singing

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.729 line:92%
and now the dancing portion."

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I went in,
and they were all --

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.866
Debbie Allen and all the
other executive producers

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
were behind a table,
and she was like, "All right."

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:12.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
We like your singing.
Now let's see your dancing."

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:16.142 size:88% position:44%
And I was like, "Okay."
And, so, just freestyle.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like,
"Just show me your moves."

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:21.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Okay, just like that?

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:22.949 line:92%
Like, no music or anything?"

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:26.286
So, she was like, "Nope.
Just show me your moves."

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.388 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So, this is what I did.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.989 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.859 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.262
Where should I do it?
-Just -- Yeah. Right over there.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.797 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-So, I have a dress --

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a dress on,
so I can't really move,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I was just like,
"Are you ready, Miss Allen?"

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.971 size:88% position:44%
And she was like, "Yes."
And I was just like...

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.875 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.891 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:13.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Holla!
-Holla! Holla.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.400 line:92%
-And, now, how did that end?

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it pretty immediate
that they asked you to leave?

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.939 line:92%
-She was like, "Thank you."

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.508 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like, that was it.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:24.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the worst.
That's a true story.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:27.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope I didn't show --
flash my undies.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a dress on,
so that was hard to do.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.219
I wish I could have moved well.
But, you know, you get the idea.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You should know that it was
better than what we saw.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was very limited
by the dress.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:40.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like that -- It was
so much better than that.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:46.566
It is always just the joy
of joys to have you here.

